  "notes": "SLC Agricola B3-listed since 2007 (largest pure-play row-crop operator in Brazil — soja/algodão/milho across 561k acres in MATOPIBA + Mato Grosso + Goiás). Calendar fiscal year (Jan-Dec). BRL reporting. IFRS reporter (CVM). grossRevenueMM = receita bruta (pre-PIS/COFINS/ICMS); revenueMM = receita líquida. Quarterly data sourced from ITR/DFP filings on CVM and earnings releases at ri.slcagricola.com.br. Annual Deloitte appraisal of OWNED cultivable land (terras próprias) with Jul base date (started disclosure in 2020). Mar-2025: Agrícola Xingu acquisition added ~27,516 ha (+5%) — drove FY25 land book step-up. Quarterly expensesBySegmentMM are approximations from ITR's classification of CPV (custos), despesas com vendas, gerais e administrativas, depreciação. Revenue segments are crop-product disclosures from quarterly releases (Receita Bruta por Produto). Some quarterly biological-asset / hedge marks contribute to EBITDA volatility. SLC restated several 2021-2022 cotton segment line items in the FY23 reference — values shown reflect the 2023 annual report's reclassified comparatives. FY 2007-FY 2019 backfill from CVM RAD DFPs + annual reports — annual only (quarterly disclosure granularity for crop segments was inconsistent pre-2020). IPO June-2007 raised R$490M. Plantadas area expanded from 145k ha (FY07) to 458k ha (FY19) via greenfield + brownfield additions in MATOPIBA. Pre-2010 figures use BRGAAP, FY2010+ use IFRS — figures shown reflect IFRS-adjusted comparatives where restated, otherwise as-filed. Algodão segment scaled up materially from FY10 onward; pre-2010 cotton was minor.",
